            {
              "id": "CVE-2025-22870",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2025-22870"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://scout.docker.com/v/CVE-2025-22870?s=golang&n=stdlib&t=golang&vr=%3C1.23.7",
              "help": {
                "text": "Matching of hosts against proxy patterns can improperly treat an IPv6 zone ID as a hostname component. For example, when the NO_PROXY environment variable is set to \"*.example.com\", a request to \"[::1%25.example.com]:80` will incorrectly match and not be proxied.\n",
                "markdown": "> Matching of hosts against proxy patterns can improperly treat an IPv6 zone ID as a hostname component. For example, when the NO_PROXY environment variable is set to \"*.example.com\", a request to \"[::1%25.example.com]:80` will incorrectly match and not be proxied.\n\n|                                          |\n|Package         pkg:golang/stdlib@1.20.7  |\n|Affected range  <1.23.7                   |\n|Fixed version   1.23.7                    |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "affected_version": "<1.23.7",
                "cvssV3_severity": "MEDIUM",
