            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-32280",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-32280"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://scout.docker.com/v/CVE-2026-32280?s=golang&n=stdlib&t=golang&vr=%3C1.25.9",
              "help": {
                "text": "During chain building, the amount of work that is done is not correctly limited when a large number of intermediate certificates are passed in VerifyOptions.Intermediates, which can lead to a denial of service. This affects both direct users of crypto/x509 and users of crypto/tls.\n",
                "markdown": "> During chain building, the amount of work that is done is not correctly limited when a large number of intermediate certificates are passed in VerifyOptions.Intermediates, which can lead to a denial of service. This affects both direct users of crypto/x509 and users of crypto/tls.\n\n|                                          |\n|Package         pkg:golang/stdlib@1.20.7  |\n|Affected range  <1.25.9                   |\n|Fixed version   1.25.9                    |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
