              "helpUri": "https://scout.docker.com/v/CVE-2026-103111?s=debian&n=pcre2&ns=debian&t=deb&osn=debian&osv=12&vr=%3C10.42-1%2Bdeb12u2",
              "help": {
                "text": "PCRE2 before 10.49, when there is an attacker-controlled regular expression and certain JIT API usage, allows an out-of-bounds write with arbitrary data.\n\n---\n- pcre2 10.48-3.1 (bug https://bugs.debian.org/cgi-bin/bugreport.cgi?bug=1149217)\nhttps://github.com/PCRE2Project/pcre2/security/advisories/GHSA-r9hj-j2rw-4q3m\nFixed by: https://github.com/PCRE2Project/pcre2/commit/2b4038298072684b0fae29b15bedfb1a75bda46d (pcre2-10.49)\n",
                "markdown": "> PCRE2 before 10.49, when there is an attacker-controlled regular expression and certain JIT API usage, allows an out-of-bounds write with arbitrary data.\n\n---\n- pcre2 10.48-3.1 (bug https://bugs.debian.org/cgi-bin/bugreport.cgi?bug=1149217)\nhttps://github.com/PCRE2Project/pcre2/security/advisories/GHSA-r9hj-j2rw-4q3m\nFixed by: https://github.com/PCRE2Project/pcre2/commit/2b4038298072684b0fae29b15bedfb1a75bda46d (pcre2-10.49)\n\n|                                                                                                        |\n|Package         pkg:deb/debian/pcre2@10.42-1%2Bdeb12u1?os_distro=bookworm&os_name=debian&os_version=12  |\n|Affected range  <10.42-1+deb12u2                                                                        |\n|Fixed version   10.42-1+deb12u2                                                                         |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
